shgrep patch for clang 23.1.4 (the same code is still on upstream main as of 2026-11-01).

clang-repl does not fully withdraw an input that fails to compile, so the C++ REPL session breaks after one bad cell:
- The partial llvm::Module stays open and the next input is generated into it. Redefining a function the failed
  input defined then fails with "definition with same mangled name ... as another definition", and the failed
  input's initializers and top-level statements would still run with the next input.
- Sema has already set the points of instantiation for the templates the failed input used, but its pending
  instantiations are discarded. Later inputs never queue them again, so their definitions stay missing and the
  cell DLL fails to link with "undefined symbol" for std::get, std::construct_at, std::_Traits_find and similar.
- An input whose decl a consumer rejects returns without any cleanup or diagnostics reset.

The fix withdraws a failed input in both error paths of IncrementalParser: it clears the pending error so CodeGen
sees the next step, finishes the pending instantiations, discards the partial module through the new
CodeGenerator::DiscardModule(), removes the input from Sema and resets the diagnostics. DiscardModule() drops the
module and the per-module CodeGen state (initializers, queued inline member functions) and makes the inline and
template code queued or emitted there pending again, so later modules emit it where they use it. Running CodeGen's
normal end-of-module step instead is not safe after an unrecoverable error.

Apply in the LLVM source folder (tag llvmorg-23.1.4; no git repository needed), then rebuild and reinstall LLVM:
  git apply <shgrep>\tools\patches\clang-23.1.4-repl-failed-input.patch
  cmake --build <LLVM build folder> --target install

diff -ru a/clang/include/clang/CodeGen/ModuleBuilder.h b/clang/include/clang/CodeGen/ModuleBuilder.h
--- a/clang/include/clang/CodeGen/ModuleBuilder.h
+++ b/clang/include/clang/CodeGen/ModuleBuilder.h
@@ -116,6 +116,13 @@
   /// Create a new \c llvm::Module after calling HandleTranslationUnit. This
   /// enable codegen in interactive processing environments.
   llvm::Module* StartModule(llvm::StringRef ModuleName, llvm::LLVMContext &C);
+
+  /// Discard the module being built, with everything emitted into it, and
+  /// start an empty module in its place. Inline and template code emitted into
+  /// the discarded module becomes pending again, so later modules emit it where
+  /// they use it. For interactive processing, when an input fails and its code
+  /// must not run.
+  llvm::Module *DiscardModule(llvm::StringRef NewModuleName);
 };
 
 /// CreateLLVMCodeGen - Create a CodeGenerator instance.
diff -ru a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CodeGenModule.cpp b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CodeGenModule.cpp
--- a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CodeGenModule.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CodeGenModule.cpp
@@ -8854,10 +8854,12 @@
   assert(NewBuilder->DeferredVTables.empty() &&
          "Newly created module should not have deferred vtables");
   NewBuilder->DeferredVTables = std::move(DeferredVTables);
+  NewBuilder->DeferredVTablesAtModuleStart = NewBuilder->DeferredVTables;
 
   assert(NewBuilder->EmittedVTables.empty() &&
          "Newly created module should not have defined vtables");
   NewBuilder->EmittedVTables = std::move(EmittedVTables);
+  NewBuilder->EmittedVTablesAtModuleStart = NewBuilder->EmittedVTables;
 
   assert(NewBuilder->MangledDeclNames.empty() &&
          "Newly created module should not have mangled decl names");
@@ -8870,6 +8872,18 @@
   NewBuilder->ABI->MangleCtx = std::move(ABI->MangleCtx);
 }
 
+void CodeGenModule::discardModuleEmissions() {
+  // Queued for this module but never emitted: emit them where used later.
+  for (const GlobalDecl &GD : DeferredDeclsToEmit)
+    DeferredDecls[getMangledName(GD)] = GD;
+  DeferredDeclsToEmit.clear();
+  // Emitted only into this module: emit them again where used later.
+  DeferredDecls.insert_range(EmittedDeferredDecls);
+  EmittedDeferredDecls.clear();
+  DeferredVTables = DeferredVTablesAtModuleStart;
+  EmittedVTables = EmittedVTablesAtModuleStart;
+}
